		(uuid "79a128de-5b27-488f-864f-eb0173504b79")
	)
	(text_box "Key points for VCN power design:\n\nVCN power is used to supply power to the eMarker or active cables, with a protocol specification of 3.3-5V±20%.\n\nThe PB8/PB10 levels are VDD5, VCN outputs about 4V, and it has overvoltage backflow protection.\n\nWhen VHV is at high voltage, the NMOS will bear the full voltage drop, so try to avoid this or pay attention to power consumption.\n\n\n\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 320.04 134.62 0)
		(size -177.8 35.56)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
			(color 255 0 0 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "74debde0-b9ca-4460-a71a-43551a9ab362")
	)
	(text_box "\nExplanation of the DCDC Input MOS (Q6) Usage:\n\nThe DCDC isn’t used in all routines. For routines that don’t use the DCDC, if you don’t disconnect it, it might cause functional issues.\n\nIn the routines, Q6 has been controlled according to its application. For new applications, you should properly configure whether the DCDC is connected to the circuit.\n\nIf your application needs the power input to always stay at high voltage/high power, then you need to use the DCDC to supply the output. If your application can work fine staying at low voltages like 5V or 9V for a long time, then you don’t need the DCDC.\n\nIf you want to use the DCDC, please use a wire to replace Q6 in the actual application.\n\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 391.16 20.32 0)
		(size -53.34 55.88)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
			(color 255 0 0 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "9a3172f9-adc7-4786-9eeb-9a1468a6e502")
	)
	(text_box "The DIP switch controls whether the corresponding CC has DeadBatt. Please configure it as needed according to your application. CCs without DeadBatt also won’t be able to enable Rd later."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 129.54 180.34 0)
		(size -109.22 15.24)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
			(color 255 0 0 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "b9cf9fc6-cd46-4160-8ac2-57c995780356")
	)
	(text_box "DCDC Output MOS (Q5) Usage:\nIn apps with a DCDC, Q5 controls if the DCDC output connects to VBUS.\n Make sure to prevent backflow both ways."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 119.38 27.94 0)
		(size -55.88 20.32)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
			(color 255 0 0 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "de659432-b4a1-476a-a189-9a15af7c26c5")
	)
